WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.750
CoParent starts with one parent.

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:06.400
Alex signs in for the first time and names the family, a synthetic one for this film.

00:00:07.002 --> 00:00:08.042
Then the children.

00:00:08.042 --> 00:00:10.642
Mia first, with her date of birth and school.

00:00:11.245 --> 00:00:12.418
Then the other parent.

00:00:12.418 --> 00:00:15.565
Alex invites Sam by email, checks everything, and finishes.

00:00:16.809 --> 00:00:19.278
Until Sam joins, the dashboard says so.

00:00:19.278 --> 00:00:25.609
Expenses and messages can already be logged for Sam, and they are waiting, unread, when Sam arrives.

00:00:27.584 --> 00:00:31.944
Sam follows the link in the email, signs in, and joins the family.

00:00:35.401 --> 00:00:36.450
A few weeks later.

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:43.561
Leo has been added, and the dashboard opens on who has the children today, the next handover, and what is waiting on Alex.

00:00:44.164 --> 00:00:45.511
The calendar is shared.

00:00:45.511 --> 00:00:52.364
Each parent's time has its own colour, and clubs, appointments and half term sit on top, repeating where they repeat.

00:00:52.966 --> 00:00:54.566
The week view shows the times.

00:00:56.792 --> 00:00:58.645
Changes are requested, not made.

00:00:58.645 --> 00:01:04.666
Sam wants to swap a weekend for a wedding, and the request shows what is booked beside what is proposed.

00:01:04.666 --> 00:01:07.792
I approve it, and the calendar changes for both of us.

00:01:08.397 --> 00:01:12.324
Messages keep the plans in one place, not buried in a group chat.

00:01:12.324 --> 00:01:14.197
I reply to Sam about half term.

00:01:15.414 --> 00:01:16.951
Some things need a formal yes.

00:01:16.951 --> 00:01:22.894
Sam asks whether Leo can go to a sleepover, and I approve it with a note, so the answer is on record for both of us.

00:01:24.203 --> 00:01:28.876
That was setting up a family in CoParent, and the calendar and messages a few weeks in.

00:01:28.876 --> 00:01:33.603
Every change to the plan is asked for and agreed, so both homes work from the same week.
